[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139475,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epithelioid haemangioma (EH) is a benign vascular neoplasm composed of well-formed capillary-sized vessels lined by plump epithelioid endothelial cells in a variable background of chronic inflammation containing numerous eosinophils.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139476,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9125/0 Epithelioid haemangioma</p>\r\n<p>9125/0 Cellular epithelioid haemangioma</p>\r\n<p>9125/0 Atypical epithelioid haemangioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139477,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E81.0Y &amp; XH10T4 Neoplastic haemangioma of other specified site &amp; Epithelioid haemangioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139478,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> angiolymphoid hyperplasia with eosinophilia; histiocytoid haemangioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139479,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cellular epithelioid haemangioma; atypical epithelioid haemangioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139480,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EH can involve the eyelid skin and superficial and deep orbital soft tissues {4008683;24676051;27171790;31768366}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139481,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Clinical signs and symptoms are related to the mass effect, and include eyelid fullness, ptosis, globe displacement/proptosis, and ocular motility restriction {24676051;27171790}. The lesion can be either poorly defined or well circumscribed on imaging {24676051;27171790}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139482,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EH may occur at any age (reported range 11&ndash;86&nbsp;years) with a peak incidence in the fourth decade of life {24676051;27171790}. There is no significant sex predilection {27171790;24676051}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139483,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139484,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EH is characterized by recurrent fusions involving the <em>FOS</em> or <em>FOSB</em> genes in as many as one&nbsp;half of cases {25043949;26135557}. <em>FOS</em>-negative and <em>FOSB</em>-negative tumours may harbour an alternative <em>GATA6</em>::<em>FOXO1</em> fusion {33318580}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139485,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Grossly, EH is circumscribed and nodular or multinodular.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139486,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EH typically manifests as a lobular or multinodular proliferation of small vessels, frequently surrounding a central small artery with more mature vessels at the periphery of the lobules {15087672;21948309;3116865}. The endothelial cells have a distinctive appearance with an abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm, large rounded nuclei, and a central nucleolus, and are associated with a pericytic layer. The endothelial cells may contain large cytoplasmic vacuoles (blister cells) and may protrude into the lumen with a tombstone pattern {15087672;21948309;10768347}. A variably intense infiltrate of lymphocytes with occasional lymphoid follicles, eosinophils, and plasma cells is noted in an oedematous stroma {3116865;15087672}. Mitotic figures are rare {15087672}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>The endothelial cells express CD31, FLI1, ERG, and to a lesser extent CD34 {15087672;26135557}. Expression of cytokeratain and EMA may be noted focally {8333560;21904630}. Expression of FOSB may be helpful in distinguishing from malignant epithelioid vascular tumours {28009608}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139487,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139488,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Diagnostic molecular pathology includes evaluation for <em>FOS</em> or <em>FOSB</em> gene rearrangements in some cases {29266025;26135557;29527734}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139489,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> lobular vascular proliferation of epithelioid endothelial cells with abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm and enlarged round nuclei; stroma with chronic inflammation and eosinophils.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> demonstration of FOSB expression or rearrangements of the <em>FOS</em> and/or <em>FOSB</em> genes may be useful in a subset of cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139490,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139491,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 266,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Complete surgical excision is the treatment of choice, but lesions may recur {26685720;24676051}. Oral propranolol has been used in several reported recurrent or incompletely excised orbital lesions in young children {22186982;26954109}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]